D('heated',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The meeting grew heated when the residents challenged the traffic plan.','居民质疑交通方案时，会议气氛变得激烈起来。')],mistakes:[m('The heated debate remained calm, with no strong disagreement or emotion.','The calm debate remained measured, with no strong disagreement or emotion.','heated debate 通常有激烈情绪或争论，与冷静平和矛盾；换成 calm debate。')],quiz:[q('heated',1,1,'A heated argument is likely to involve?','strong emotion and disagreement','a room kept at a low temperature only','a silent agreement by everyone','heated 用于争论时表示激烈、情绪化。'),q('heated',1,1,'Which event could lead to a heated discussion?','two groups strongly disagree over a policy','everyone accepts the same plan without comment','a meeting is cancelled before it starts','强烈意见冲突容易引发 heated discussion。'),q('heated',1,1,'A heated exchange between colleagues is?','an emotionally intense conversation','a quiet exchange of winter coats','a measured temperature reading','heated exchange 描写激烈的言语交锋。'),q('heated',1,1,'Choose the most natural collocation.','a heated debate','a heated gratitude','a heated staircase of opinions','heated 常与 debate、argument、discussion 搭配。')]});
D('heater',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'We placed a small electric heater near the desk during the cold snap.','寒潮期间，我们在书桌旁放了一台小电暖器。')],mistakes:[m('The heater made the room colder by warming the air.','The heater made the room warmer by warming the air.','加热空气会让房间变暖而非变冷；把 colder 改为 warmer。')],quiz:[q('heater',1,1,'An electric heater is a device used to?','make a room or object warmer','cool food below freezing','measure the speed of wind','heater 是用来加热或取暖的装置。'),q('heater',1,1,'If the heater is broken on a cold night, the room may?','fail to warm up','become a swimming pool','lose its windows','heater 损坏会影响房间取暖。'),q('heater',1,1,'Which verb naturally goes with heater?','turn on','bake out of','listen at','turn on the heater 是打开取暖器的自然搭配。'),q('heater',1,1,'A portable heater can be moved because it is?','designed to be carried from place to place','part of a fixed mountain','a type of heart surgery','portable heater 指可移动的取暖器。')]});
D('heave',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'The guards heaved a stone block away from the blocked entrance.','守卫们用力把石块从被堵住的入口移开。'),ex(4,'The rough crossing made the passengers heave with nausea.','颠簸的航程让乘客们恶心得干呕。')],mistakes:[m('The boat heaved in the rough sea but remained completely motionless.','The boat rose and fell with the rough sea.','heave 描述起伏或颠簸，与完全静止矛盾；改为 rose and fell 直接描述起伏。')],quiz:[q('heave',1,1,'The workers heaved the crate onto the truck. They?','lifted or pulled it with effort','painted it carefully','measured its temperature','heave 可表示费力举起或拉动重物。'),q('heave',2,2,'Someone heaved a stone at the wall. What did they do?','threw the stone forcefully','placed the stone gently on a shelf','carved a picture into the stone','heave 可表示用力投掷重物。'),q('heave',3,3,'In the storm, the boat heaved on the waves. It?','rose and fell repeatedly','stayed perfectly still','flew above the water','heave 作不及物动词可表示起伏颠簸。'),q('heave',5,5,'With one heave, she raised the lid. What was the heave?','an effortful lift','a quiet greeting','a measured pause','名词 heave 可指奋力举起的一下。')]});
D('heaven',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'They hoped their grandmother had found peace in heaven.','他们希望祖母在天堂获得了安宁。'),ex(2,'By dawn the clouds cleared and the heavens filled with stars.','黎明时云散了，满天星斗。'),ex(3,'For a tired gardener, a quiet afternoon among the flowers was heaven.','对疲惫的园丁来说，在花丛中度过安静的下午简直是天堂。')],mistakes:[m('In the story, the characters believed that heaven was a very unpleasant place of punishment after death.','In the story, the characters believed that hell was a very unpleasant place of punishment after death.','宗教语境中的 heaven 与 hell 相反；用 hell 替换。')],quiz:[q('heaven',1,1,'In some religions, heaven is believed to be?','a place where good people go after death','a weather station above the clouds','a court hearing room','此处对应 heaven 的宗教义项。'),q('heaven',2,2,'“Stars filled the heavens” describes?','the night sky','a group of court judges','the ceiling of a small room','the heavens 可指天空、苍穹。'),q('heaven',3,3,'A quiet beach described as heaven on earth is?','an extremely pleasant place','a dangerous storm shelter','a legal inheritance','比喻义 heaven 指令人极愉快的地方或状态。'),q('heaven',1,1,'Which phrase refers to the religious afterlife sense?','believe someone is in heaven','look up at the heavens','call a holiday heaven on earth','in heaven 对应宗教上的天堂义。')]});
D('heavens',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Thank heavens the rescue team found the hikers before nightfall.','谢天谢地，救援队在天黑前找到了徒步者。')],mistakes:[m('Thank heavens, the hikers were lost forever and no one could find them.','Thank heavens, the hikers were found safely and no one was hurt.','thank heavens 表达庆幸，后接永远失踪与庆幸不协调；改成安全获救。')],quiz:[q('heavens',1,1,'In “Stars filled the heavens,” heavens means?','the sky','a person’s inheritance','a fireplace floor','heavens 是 heaven 的复数形式，可指天空。'),q('heavens',1,1,'“Thank heavens you are safe” expresses?','relief and gratitude','anger at the person','a formal court ruling','thank heavens 是表达庆幸的感叹语。'),q('heavens',1,1,'Which spelling correctly completes “The ___ opened and rain poured down”?','heavens','heavenes','heavenses','heavens 是标准拼写，也出现在 the heavens opened 中。'),q('heavens',1,1,'The phrase “look up at the heavens” directs someone to look at?','the sky above','the ground below their feet','a courtroom document','the heavens 可指头顶的天空。')]});
D('heavily',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The gate swung heavily on its old hinges and struck the wall.','大门在老旧的铰链上沉重地摆动，撞到了墙。'),ex(1,'Rain fell heavily throughout the night.','整夜都下着大雨。')],mistakes:[m('It rained heavily, with only a few drops falling in the entire valley.','It rained lightly, with only a few drops falling in the entire valley.','heavily 描述雨量大，与只有几滴矛盾；换成 lightly。')],quiz:[q('heavily',1,1,'If a door closes heavily, it moves?','with great weight or force','without making any movement','in a way that is completely weightless','heavily 可表示沉重地或用力地。'),q('heavily',1,1,'“It rained heavily” means?','a lot of rain fell','no rain fell','the rain was measured by weight','rain heavily 是下大雨。'),q('heavily',1,1,'Which sentence uses the adverb naturally?','The old box was heavily loaded.','The old box was heavy loadedly.','The old box heavily was load.','heavily 可修饰 loaded，表示装得很重。'),q('heavily',1,1,'A heavily guarded entrance has?','many guards or strong security','no guards at all','a very light door only','heavily guarded 表示戒备森严。')]});
D('heavy',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'Heavy snow closed the mountain road before sunrise.','日出前，大雪封闭了山路。'),ex(3,'He carried the news with a heavy heart.','他心情沉重地带来了这个消息。'),ex(4,'After two night shifts, the nurses faced a heavy workload.','连续上了两个夜班后，护士们面临繁重的工作量。')],mistakes:[m('The heavy suitcase weighed almost nothing and was effortless to lift.','The light suitcase weighed almost nothing and was effortless to lift.','几乎没有重量、轻易可提起与 heavy 相反；换成 light。')],quiz:[q('heavy',1,1,'A heavy suitcase is difficult to lift because it?','weighs a lot','is made only of paper','contains no objects','heavy 的基本义是重量大。'),q('heavy',2,2,'Heavy traffic on the bridge means?','many vehicles or severe congestion','the bridge is made of stone','the cars are all carrying weights','heavy 可表示数量或强度大，heavy traffic 指交通繁忙。'),q('heavy',3,3,'A person with a heavy heart feels?','sad or troubled','physically taller','hungry for a large meal','heavy heart 是心情沉重的表达。'),q('heavy',4,4,'A heavy workload requires?','a great deal of effort or work','no time or responsibility','a very light bag','heavy workload 指繁重的工作量。')]});
D('hectare',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The orchard covers six hectares on the southern slope.','这片果园占据南坡六公顷土地。'),ex(2,'The wildfire burned through more than two thousand hectares of woodland.','野火烧毁了两千多公顷林地。')],mistakes:[m('The field measures one hectare, or one hundred square metres.','The field measures one hectare, or ten thousand square metres.','一公顷等于一万平方米，不是一百平方米；更正数值即可。')],quiz:[q('hectare',1,1,'One hectare is equal to?','10,000 square metres','100 square metres','1,000 kilometres','hectare 是等于一万平方米的面积单位。'),q('hectare',2,2,'A forestry report says a fire damaged 300 hectares. It measures?','the area of land affected','the number of trees per hectare only','the height of the smoke','公顷用于测量森林等土地面积。'),q('hectare',1,1,'A farm of 12 hectares has an area of?','120,000 square metres','12 square metres','1,200,000 kilometres','12 公顷等于 12 × 10,000 平方米。'),q('hectare',1,1,'Which abbreviation may represent hectare?','ha','kg','km/h','ha 是 hectare 的常用缩写。')]});
D('hectic',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The station had a hectic morning as three delayed trains arrived together.','三列晚点列车同时到站，车站度过了忙乱的早晨。'),ex(2,'The patient had a hectic flush across her cheeks during the fever.','病人发烧时双颊泛起病态的潮红。')],mistakes:[m('After a hectic week with nothing to do and no activity, she felt refreshed.','After a quiet week with nothing to do and no activity, she felt refreshed.','hectic 表示忙乱繁忙，与无事可做相反；改成 quiet。')],quiz:[q('hectic',1,1,'A hectic schedule contains?','many activities and little free time','no appointments or tasks','only long periods of sleep','hectic 指忙碌、活动很多的状态。'),q('hectic',2,2,'A hectic flush on someone’s cheeks is associated with?','fever and a flushed appearance','a new hairstyle','a cold metal surface','hectic 也可在医学语境形容发热时的潮红。'),q('hectic',1,1,'Which phrase is natural?','a hectic day at work','a hecticly day at work','a hectic of day at work','hectic 是形容词，可直接修饰 day。'),q('hectic',1,1,'If a week is hectic, the person likely feels?','very busy and rushed','completely idle','unable to recognize faces','繁忙而忙乱的节奏是 hectic 的核心含义。')]});
D('hedge',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'Some investors use government bonds as a hedge against market losses.','一些投资者用政府债券作为对冲市场损失的手段。'),ex(4,'Asked whether he would resign, the minister hedged and gave no clear answer.','被问到是否辞职时，部长含糊其辞，没有给出明确答复。')],mistakes:[m('The gardener planted a hedge around the lawn, leaving a continuous open gap that enclosed nothing.','The gardener planted a hedge around the lawn, forming a boundary around it.','树篱围住草坪却又留出连续缺口、什么也没围住，前后矛盾；改为形成边界。')],quiz:[q('hedge',1,1,'A hedge around a garden is?','a row of bushes forming a boundary','a paved road through a city','a roof made of glass','名词 hedge 可指作为边界的一排灌木。'),q('hedge',2,2,'An investment described as a hedge against inflation is intended to?','reduce the risk of losing value','guarantee the highest possible profit','decorate a garden wall','hedge 比喻可指防范风险的手段。'),q('hedge',3,3,'To hedge a field with hawthorn is to?','surround it with a row of hawthorn bushes','remove every tree from it','measure it in hectares','hedge 作动词可表示用树篱围住。'),q('hedge',4,4,'When a speaker hedges on a question, the speaker?','avoids giving a direct answer','answers clearly and firmly','asks the audience to leave','hedge 可表示含糊其辞、避免正面回答。')]});
D('heed',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The hikers heeded the warning and turned back before the storm arrived.','徒步者们听从了警告，在暴风雨到来前折返。')],mistakes:[m('The driver heeded the warning sign and deliberately ignored it.','The driver saw the warning sign and deliberately ignored it.','heed 表示留心并听从，故与 deliberately ignored it 冲突；改为 saw。')],quiz:[q('heed',1,1,'To heed a warning is to?','pay attention to it and take it seriously','erase it from a sign','repeat it without understanding','heed 表示注意并认真对待。'),q('heed',1,1,'Which phrase is a common way to express attention to advice?','heed the advice','heed at the advice','heedly the advice','heed 可直接带宾语，表示留心或听从。'),q('heed',1,1,'If a pilot heeds the weather alert, the pilot may?','change the flight plan for safety','pretend the alert was a passenger','turn the alert into a map','听从天气警报可能促使飞行员调整计划。'),q('heed',1,1,'Choose the correct form: She ___ the doctor’s advice.','heeded','heed','heeding','heed 的过去式是规则形式 heeded。')]});
D('heedless',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Heedless of the slippery steps, the courier rushed down carrying two boxes.','快递员不顾台阶湿滑，抱着两个箱子匆忙跑下去。')],mistakes:[m('Heedless of the warning, she carefully obeyed it.','Mindful of the warning, she carefully obeyed it.','heedless of 表示不留意、不顾及，与认真遵循该警告矛盾；mindful of 是最小替换。')],quiz:[q('heedless',1,1,'A heedless pedestrian crosses without checking the traffic. The pedestrian is?','not paying attention','carefully observing every vehicle','directing the traffic','heedless 指不留神、不注意。'),q('heedless',1,1,'“Heedless of danger” means?','not considering the danger','fully protected from every danger','warning other people about danger','heedless of 表示不顾、没注意到危险。'),q('heedless',1,1,'Which adjective is closest to heedless in this context?','inattentive','alert','cautious','inattentive 是不专心、不留意的近义词。'),q('heedless',1,1,'A heedless mistake is most likely made?','without proper attention','after careful checking','by following a detailed checklist','heedless 可描述因粗心而发生的行为或错误。')]});
D('heel',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'The dancer changed into flat shoes after the narrow heel began to hurt.','细鞋跟开始让她疼痛后，舞者换上了平底鞋。'),ex(4,'The sailing boat heeled sharply when a gust struck its sails.','一阵风吹动船帆时，帆船猛地向一侧倾斜。')],mistakes:[m('The boat heeled upright from side to side while remaining perfectly level and still.','The boat rocked from side to side while remaining unsteady in the water.','heel 指倾斜，perfectly level and still 与之相矛盾；换用 rocked 并去掉 still。')],quiz:[q('heel',1,1,'The heel of your foot is?','the rounded back part','the toes at the front','the middle of the palm','heel 可指脚后跟。'),q('heel',2,2,'A shoe with a high heel has?','a raised part under the back of the shoe','a raised part under the toes only','no sole at all','鞋 heel 是鞋底后部隆起的鞋跟。'),q('heel',3,3,'A trained dog heeled beside its handler. It?','followed closely at the handler’s side','ran away to find food','sat on the handler’s shoulder','heel 作动词可表示紧随其后。'),q('heel',5,5,'The heel of a loaf is?','an end piece of the bread','the middle slice','a kitchen knife','heel 也可指一条面包的端头或剩下的一块。')]});
D('height',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'From the height above the valley, the hikers could see the river bend.','从山谷上方的高处，徒步者们看到了河流的弯道。'),ex(3,'At the height of the festival, every square in town was crowded.','节日期间最热闹的时候，镇上每个广场都挤满了人。')],mistakes:[m('The height of the tower is its width from side to side, not its vertical measurement.','The width of the tower is its measurement from side to side, not its height.','height 是垂直尺寸，side-to-side 指宽度；交换术语并保持解释一致。')],quiz:[q('height',1,1,'A person’s height measures?','how tall the person is','how much the person weighs','how quickly the person walks','height 可指人的身高。'),q('height',2,2,'From a great height, you are looking from?','a high place','a deep underground tunnel','the center of a lake','height 可指高处或高地。'),q('height',3,3,'At the height of summer means?','during the most intense or central part of summer','before winter begins','at the top of a tall building','at the height of 表示某事达到顶点或最盛时期。'),q('height',1,1,'Which spelling is correct?','height','heighth','hight','标准拼写是 height；不是 heighth。')]});
D('heighten',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The sudden silence heightened the audience’s curiosity.','突然的寂静增强了观众的好奇心。')],mistakes:[m('New evidence heightened suspicion but reduced it to zero.','New evidence increased suspicion rather than reducing it.','heighten 表示增强，与把怀疑降为零矛盾；改为 increased 保留增强之义。')],quiz:[q('heighten',1,1,'A sound that heightens tension makes the tension?','stronger','lower in physical position','completely absent','heighten 可表示增强某种程度或情绪。'),q('heighten',1,1,'The new evidence heightened suspicion. What happened to suspicion?','It increased.','It disappeared.','It was measured in metres.','heighten suspicion 表示使怀疑加深。'),q('heighten',1,1,'Which sentence uses heighten naturally?','The warning heightened public concern.','The warning heighted public concern.','The warning heightenedly public concern.','heighten 的过去式是 heightened。'),q('heighten',1,1,'A writer may heighten suspense by?','delaying the reveal of a crucial fact','explaining the ending in the first line','removing every source of uncertainty','延迟揭示关键信息会增强悬念。')]});
D('heir',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'As the only heir to the farm, Lena inherited the land and its equipment.','作为农场的唯一继承人，莉娜继承了土地和设备。'),ex(2,'The young director was seen as the heir to her mentor’s artistic tradition.','这位年轻导演被视为其导师艺术传统的继承者。')],mistakes:[m('He was the heir to the estate, but had no legal right to inherit any of it.','He was the heir to the estate and had the legal right to inherit it.','heir 的法律义指有权继承的人，与无权继承冲突；改为肯定。')],quiz:[q('heir',1,1,'An heir to an estate is someone who?','has the legal right to inherit it','sold the estate to its owner','built the estate’s road','heir 可指依法有权继承财产的人。'),q('heir',2,2,'An heir to a musical tradition is a person who?','continues or carries on that tradition','inherits a music studio by law only','refuses to perform any music','比喻义 heir 指承接传统或事业的人。'),q('heir',1,1,'Which phrase commonly uses heir?','the heir to the throne','the heir on the weather','the heir under a melody','heir 常与 to 连用，表示某项财产或地位的继承者。'),q('heir',1,1,'Heir is pronounced like which common word?','air','haircut','here','heir 与 air 同音。')]});
D('helical',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'A helical staircase winds around a narrow central column.','一座螺旋楼梯围绕着狭窄的中央立柱盘旋而上。')],mistakes:[m('The helical spring was a straight, flat rod with no turns.','The straight spring was a flat rod with no turns.','helical 表示螺旋形，完全笔直且没有弯曲与之矛盾；改用 straight。')],quiz:[q('helical',1,1,'A helical staircase is shaped like?','a spiral winding upward','a flat square with no turns','a straight horizontal line','helical 指呈螺旋形的。'),q('helical',1,1,'A helical structure resembles the shape of?','a screw thread','a perfect cube','a flat sheet of paper','螺纹呈螺旋形，是 helical 的典型形状。'),q('helical',1,1,'Which object could naturally be called helical?','a coiled spring','a smooth glass pane','a straight ruler','盘绕的弹簧具有螺旋形状。'),q('helical',1,1,'Choose the correctly formed adjective.','helical','helixal','helixly','helical 是表示螺旋形的标准形容词。')]});
D('helicopter',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'A helicopter hovered above the mountain hut until the rescue crew was ready.','救援人员准备就绪前，一架直升机在山间小屋上空盘旋。'),ex(2,'The injured climber was helicoptered to a hospital in the nearest city.','受伤的登山者被直升机送往最近城市的医院。')],mistakes:[m('The helicopter flew using fixed wings alone and had no rotating blades.','The airplane flew using fixed wings alone and had no rotating blades.','helicopter 靠旋翼飞行，固定翼且无旋翼与之矛盾；用 airplane 替换。')],quiz:[q('helicopter',1,1,'A helicopter differs from a typical airplane because it flies using?','large rotating blades','a sail and underwater fins','a hot-air balloon only','直升机依靠旋翼产生升力。'),q('helicopter',2,2,'If rescuers helicopter a patient to hospital, they?','transport the patient by helicopter','ask the patient to repair a helicopter','leave the patient at the scene','helicopter 作动词可表示用直升机运送。'),q('helicopter',1,1,'Which situation most likely calls for a helicopter?','reaching an isolated mountain rescue site','sailing across a shallow harbor','traveling through an underground tunnel','直升机适合抵达偏远的救援地点。'),q('helicopter',1,1,'What is a common shortened informal name for a helicopter?','copter','helic','heliport','copter 可作 helicopter 的口语简称。')]});
D('helix',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The wire formed a helix around the narrow glass tube.','铁丝围绕细玻璃管形成了一个螺旋。')],mistakes:[m('The wire formed a helix as a single perfectly straight line with no curves.','The wire formed a straight line with no curves.','helix 是螺旋曲线，不可能同时是完全笔直且无弯曲；用 straight line 替换。')],quiz:[q('helix',1,1,'A helix is a curve shaped like?','a three-dimensional spiral','a flat straight line','a closed square','helix 指螺旋状曲线。'),q('helix',1,1,'The double helix is a well-known description of?','DNA’s structure','the shape of a flat window','a type of courtroom','DNA 常被描述为双螺旋结构。'),q('helix',1,1,'Which object could trace a helix?','a spring coiled around a cylinder','a ruler laid flat','a square tile','绕圆柱盘绕的弹簧可呈螺旋形。'),q('helix',1,1,'Choose a correct plural form given in the entry.','helixes','helixs','helixies','该词条列出的 helix 复数形式是 helixes。')]});
D('hell',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'In the legend, the gate to hell stood beneath the ruined city.','传说中，通往地狱的大门位于废墟城市下方。'),ex(2,'The weeks without clean water became a living hell for the villagers.','没有干净水的那几周对村民来说简直是人间地狱。'),ex(3,'What the hell happened to the lights?','这些灯到底怎么了？')],mistakes:[m('After the ceasefire, the city became a living hell of safety, comfort, and peace for everyone.','After the ceasefire, the city became a peaceful refuge of safety, comfort, and peace for everyone.','living hell 表示极其痛苦的处境，与安全舒适和平相矛盾；替换为 peaceful refuge。')],quiz:[q('hell',1,1,'In some religions, hell is described as?','a place of punishment after death','a ship’s steering wheel','a type of flowering garden','hell 的宗教义指死后受罚之所。'),q('hell',2,2,'If a difficult period was “a living hell,” it was?','extremely unpleasant and painful','a relaxing vacation','a short and easy task','比喻义 hell 可表示极其痛苦的处境。'),q('hell',3,3,'In “What the hell is going on?”, hell is used to?','add emphasis or express anger','name a person’s inheritance','describe a calm greeting','what the hell 是带强调或恼怒色彩的口语表达。'),q('hell',2,2,'Which context uses hell metaphorically?','The endless delays made the trip a hell.','The priest described a religious belief about hell.','The old map labeled a place as hell.','旅行因不断延误而痛苦，是 hell 的比喻义。')]});
D('hello',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'She smiled and said hello to the new student at the door.','她在门口微笑着向新同学问好。'),ex(2,'Hello, could you tell me when the next bus leaves?','喂，请问您能告诉我下一班公交什么时候发车吗？'),ex(3,'The host gave each guest a warm hello at the entrance.','主人在入口处热情地向每位客人打招呼。')],mistakes:[m('She said hello to the caller after hanging up and ending the conversation.','She said goodbye to the caller after hanging up and ending the conversation.','挂断并结束通话时应道别而非问候；把 hello 换成 goodbye。')],quiz:[q('hello',1,1,'When you meet a classmate, you might say hello as?','a greeting','a court sentence','a unit of land area','hello 常用作见面时的问候语。'),q('hello',2,2,'A person answers the phone with “Hello?” to?','begin the telephone conversation','end the call without speaking','report the caller’s height','hello 可用于接听电话时应答。'),q('hello',3,3,'A warm hello is?','a friendly greeting','a cold medical device','a formal inheritance document','hello 作名词可指一次问候或招呼。'),q('hello',1,1,'Which phrase is natural when greeting a friend?','say hello to Maya','say hello Maya to','say a hellos to Maya','常见结构是 say hello to someone。')]});
D('helm',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The captain held the helm as the ship entered the narrow channel.','船驶入狭窄水道时，船长握着舵轮。')],mistakes:[m('The captain took the helm but left the ship’s steering wheel untouched and unattended.','The captain took the helm and steered the ship through the channel.','helm 是船舶操舵装置；掌舵却不碰舵且无人操控相矛盾。')],quiz:[q('helm',1,1,'A ship’s helm is used to?','steer the ship','measure the depth of the sea','raise the sails only','helm 指掌控船舶方向的舵或舵轮。'),q('helm',1,1,'A captain at the helm is?','in control of the ship’s steering','standing on the ship’s roof','counting the passengers','at the helm 可指掌舵，也可引申为负责掌控。'),q('helm',1,1,'Which phrase uses helm figuratively?','She took the helm of the company.','She painted the company’s hull blue.','She dropped the ship’s anchor.','take the helm 可比喻接掌领导或控制权。'),q('helm',1,1,'Which object is most directly connected with a helm?','a ship’s steering wheel','a courtroom gavel','a garden hedge','helm 与船舶操舵有关。')]});
D('helmet',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The construction crew wore helmets while working beneath the scaffold.','施工队在脚手架下作业时都戴着安全帽。'),ex(2,'The firefighter’s helmet covered his face with a clear heat-resistant visor.','消防员的防护头盔带有透明耐热面罩，遮住了他的脸。')],mistakes:[m('The cyclist wore a helmet that left the entire head unprotected.','The cyclist wore a helmet that protected the entire head.','helmet 的用途是保护头部；完全不防护与其功能矛盾。')],quiz:[q('helmet',1,1,'Why should a cyclist wear a helmet?','to protect the head in a fall','to improve the bicycle’s speed','to keep the tires inflated','helmet 是保护头部的硬质帽子。'),q('helmet',2,2,'A firefighter’s helmet may include a protective?','visor or mask','shoe heel','steering wheel','helmet 的扩展义可指防毒、防火的面罩或罩。'),q('helmet',1,1,'Which collocation is natural?','wear a safety helmet','wear a safety helmetry','wear a safety of helmet','wear a helmet 是自然搭配。'),q('helmet',1,1,'A hard hat on a building site is another kind of?','helmet','hearth','helicopter','安全帽属于保护头部的 helmet。')]});
D('help',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'A clearer map would help the visitors find the clinic.','更清楚的地图会帮助访客找到诊所。'),ex(3,'I could not help smiling when the puppy chased its tail.','小狗追着自己的尾巴跑时，我忍不住笑了。'),ex(5,'The technician was a great help during the power failure.','停电期间，那位技术员帮了大忙。')],mistakes:[m('The guide helped the tourists find the station, but did not assist them in any way.','The guide helped the tourists find the station and assisted them.','helped them find 本身就是协助，与 did not assist 冲突；改为肯定。')],quiz:[q('help',1,1,'Can you help me carry these boxes? The speaker asks someone to?','make carrying them easier','buy new boxes','measure the boxes','help someone do something means assist them.'),q('help',2,2,'A brighter lamp may help you read. It may?','make reading easier','prevent you from seeing the page','change the words on the page','help 可表示有助于改善情形。'),q('help',3,3,'“I can’t help laughing” means?','I cannot stop myself from laughing','I refuse to laugh at all','I can repair someone’s laughter','can’t help doing 表示忍不住做某事。'),q('help',4,4,'“Thank you for your help” refers to?','the assistance you gave','your height','your heartbeat','help 作名词可指帮助或援助。')]});
D('helper',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Each volunteer helper received a badge before the community event began.','社区活动开始前，每位志愿帮手都领到了一枚徽章。')],mistakes:[m('The helper refused to assist anyone and made every task harder.','The obstacle refused to assist anyone and made every task harder.','helper 指提供帮助的人；拒绝帮忙反而添乱与 helper 的命名不符，换成 obstacle。')],quiz:[q('helper',1,1,'A helper at a community event is someone who?','assists with the tasks','audits the event’s land area','steers a helicopter','helper 指提供帮助的人。'),q('helper',1,1,'If a teacher asks for a classroom helper, the teacher wants?','a person to help with classroom jobs','a new piece of furniture','a written court ruling','helper 是帮手、助手。'),q('helper',1,1,'Choose the correct plural.','helpers','helperes','helperies','helper 的复数形式是 helpers。'),q('helper',1,1,'Which sentence uses helper as a noun?','The helper carried the boxes.','They helpered the boxes.','The helperly box was heavy.','helper 是表示人的名词。')]});
D('helpful',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The station clerk gave us helpful directions to the museum entrance.','车站工作人员给了我们前往博物馆入口的实用指引。')],mistakes:[m('The instructions were helpful, but they gave no useful information at all.','The instructions were unhelpful, because they gave no useful information.','helpful 表示有帮助，与完全没有有用信息矛盾；加 un- 并合并因果。')],quiz:[q('helpful',1,1,'A helpful instruction is one that?','makes a task easier to do','hides every necessary step','is unrelated to the task','helpful 表示有帮助、能使事情更容易。'),q('helpful',1,1,'The phrase “helpful to beginners” means useful?','for people who are new to the subject','only for people who wrote the book','for measuring a person’s height','helpful to someone 表示对某人有帮助。'),q('helpful',1,1,'Which is the natural opposite of helpful?','unhelpful','helpfully','helper','unhelpful 表示没有帮助的。'),q('helpful',1,1,'A helpful guide at a station might?','explain which platform to use','remove every station sign','refuse to answer any question','提供清晰指引的工作人员很有帮助。')]});
D('helping',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'After finishing her soup, Mina asked for a second helping of rice.','喝完汤后，米娜又要了一份米饭。')],mistakes:[m('He asked for a second helping but received no extra portion of food.','He asked for a second helping and received an extra portion of food.','a second helping 指再来一份食物，却说没有多给一份；改为肯定。')],quiz:[q('helping',1,1,'A second helping at dinner is?','another portion of food','a second person offering advice','a repeated court hearing','helping 可数时指一份盛出的食物。'),q('helping',1,1,'If someone takes a large helping of rice, they take?','a large serving','a small spoon made of metal','a map of the dining room','a helping 指一份食物，常译为一份或一盘。'),q('helping',1,1,'Which sentence uses helping as a noun?','She served me a helping of vegetables.','She helping the vegetables yesterday.','The vegetables were helpingly green.','a helping of vegetables 是自然的名词短语。'),q('helping',1,1,'The waiter offered another helping after the guest finished the first. The guest could receive?','an additional serving','a medical examination','a new bicycle helmet','another helping 意为再来一份。')]});
D('hemisphere',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The expedition crossed the southern hemisphere during the austral summer.','探险队在南半球的南半球夏季期间穿越了该区域。'),ex(2,'The scan showed activity in the left hemisphere of the patient’s brain.','扫描显示患者大脑左半球有活动。'),ex(3,'Her research opened a new hemisphere of ideas about language learning.','她的研究为语言学习开辟了新的思想领域。')],mistakes:[m('The equator divides Earth into its eastern and western hemispheres.','The equator divides Earth into its northern and southern hemispheres.','赤道将地球分为南北半球；东西半球通常按本初子午线划分。')],quiz:[q('hemisphere',1,1,'The equator divides Earth into which hemispheres?','the northern and southern hemispheres','the left and right brain hemispheres','the upper and lower oceans','地理义 hemisphere 指地球的一半，赤道划分南北半球。'),q('hemisphere',2,2,'The left hemisphere mentioned in a brain scan is?','one half of the brain','one half of the Earth','a region of a courtroom','hemisphere 也指大脑的两个半球之一。'),q('hemisphere',3,3,'A hemisphere of ideas means?','a broad area of thought or activity','a physical half of a planet only','a type of medical scan','hemisphere 可比喻活动或知识领域。'),q('hemisphere',1,1,'What is the plural of hemisphere?','hemispheres','hemispheries','hemisphers','hemisphere 的标准复数是 hemispheres。')]});
D('hen',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The hen settled back onto the nest after collecting straw for it.','母鸡衔来稻草后又回到窝里趴下。'),ex(2,'A hen pheasant led her chicks through the grass.','一只雌雉带着小雉鸡穿过草丛。')],mistakes:[m('The rooster laid three eggs in the nesting box.','The hen laid three eggs in the nesting box.','下蛋的是母鸡而非公鸡；把 rooster 换成 hen。')],quiz:[q('hen',1,1,'A hen is an adult female?','chicken','horse','eagle only','hen 的常见义是成年母鸡。'),q('hen',2,2,'A hen pheasant is?','a female pheasant','a young male pheasant','a rooster','hen 可泛指其他鸟类的雌鸟。'),q('hen',1,1,'Which animal is most likely to lay eggs in a henhouse?','a hen','a bull','a ram','母鸡通常在 henhouse 里产蛋。'),q('hen',1,1,'Choose the correct plural.','hens','henes','hennies','hen 的复数形式是 hens。')]});
D('hence',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The bridge is closed, hence the long detour through the village.','桥梁封闭了，因此车辆要绕行村庄，路程也更长。'),ex(2,'The lease ends six months hence, so we have time to find a new flat.','租约六个月后到期，所以我们有时间找新公寓。')],mistakes:[m('The roads were icy, hence the bus arrived early because the driver drove slowly.','The roads were icy, hence the bus arrived late because the driver drove slowly.','路面结冰且司机开得慢，通常导致晚到；把 early 改为 late。')],quiz:[q('hence',1,1,'“The road is closed, hence the delay” means the delay happened?','for that reason','at a point five years from now','because the road is wider','hence 可表示因此、由此。'),q('hence',2,2,'“Two weeks hence” means?','two weeks from now','two weeks ago','at two o’clock today','时间义 hence 表示从现在起经过一段时间。'),q('hence',1,1,'Which construction is natural in formal writing?','The data were incomplete, hence the caution.','The data were incomplete, hence of the caution.','The data were incomplete, hence cautioning.','hence 后可直接接名词短语，表示因此。'),q('hence',1,1,'Which word is closest to hence in “hence the name”?','therefore','beforehand','yesterday','此处 hence 与 therefore 意思相近。')]});
D('henceforth',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Henceforth, visitors must sign in at the reception desk.','从今以后，访客必须在接待处登记。'),ex(2,'The agreement states that the supplier will henceforth be referred to as “the Vendor.”','协议规定，供应方以下简称“卖方”。')],mistakes:[m('Henceforth, the new rule applied only once last year and no longer applies.','Previously, the new rule applied only once last year and no longer applies.','henceforth 表示从现在起往后，与只发生在去年且已停止不符；改为 previously。')],quiz:[q('henceforth',1,1,'A notice says “Henceforth, badges must be displayed.” When must this rule begin?','from now on','only before the notice was written','one week in the past','henceforth 表示从此以后。'),q('henceforth',2,2,'In a contract, “henceforth referred to as the Buyer” means?','the document will use Buyer as the name from this point onward','the Buyer has already left the contract','the Buyer is a witness to the contract only','公文中 henceforth 引出以下简称或之后的称谓。'),q('henceforth',1,1,'Which phrase is a less formal equivalent of henceforth?','from now on','long ago','at the same time yesterday','from now on 是日常语体的近义说法。'),q('henceforth',1,1,'Which register best fits henceforth?','formal written language','casual text-message slang','a children’s animal sound','henceforth 常用于正式书面文本。')]});
D('her',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Her jacket was hanging beside the classroom door.','她的夹克挂在教室门旁。'),ex(2,'The receptionist gave her a map of the museum.','接待员给了她一张博物馆地图。')],mistakes:[m('The receptionist gave she a map and asked her to find the gallery.','The receptionist gave her a map and asked her to find the gallery.','give 后的宾语用宾格 her，而不是主格 she。')],quiz:[q('her',1,1,'In “her jacket,” her tells us the jacket?','belongs to or is associated with a female person','belongs to the person being spoken to','belongs to a group of men','限定词 her 表示“她的”。'),q('her',2,2,'In “I called her,” her is?','the object form of she','the possessive form of they','the subject form of he','her 可作 she 的宾格。'),q('her',1,1,'Choose the correct phrase.','her own notebook','hers own notebook','she own notebook','her 作限定词修饰 notebook；hers 不直接修饰名词。'),q('her',2,2,'Which sentence uses her as an object pronoun?','We invited her to dinner.','Her coat is blue.','She arrived after lunch.','invited 后需要宾语，使用宾格 her。')]});
D('herald',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The first warm evenings heralded the arrival of spring.','最初几个温暖的夜晚预示着春天到来。'),ex(3,'A herald announced the visitors before they entered the hall.','来客进入大厅前，一名传令官先通报了他们。'),ex(4,'The first robin is often seen as a herald of spring.','知更鸟常被视为春天来临的先兆。')],mistakes:[m('The first snow heralded the arrival of summer, even though winter had just begun.','The first snow heralded the arrival of winter, even though winter had just begun.','初雪出现在冬季开始时，预示夏天到来不合时序；改为 winter。')],quiz:[q('herald',1,1,'Dark clouds can herald a storm by?','giving a sign that it is coming','stopping all weather changes','recording the storm after it ends','动词 herald 表示预示某事即将发生。'),q('herald',2,2,'A new medicine was heralded as a breakthrough. It was?','publicly announced or praised as one','hidden from all patients','used to measure a ship','herald 可表示公开宣称或誉为。'),q('herald',3,3,'In a historical story, a herald might?','carry a message and announce visitors','repair a farm fence','inherit a throne','herald 可指传令官或报信者。'),q('herald',4,4,'A herald of spring is?','a sign that spring is coming','a person who stops spring','a winter storm that has ended','名词 herald 可指某事即将来临的先兆。')]});
D('herb',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The cook chopped fresh herbs and stirred them into the soup.','厨师把新鲜香草切碎，拌进汤里。'),ex(2,'The family asked an herbalist about the traditional medicinal herb.','这家人向草药师咨询了这种传统药草。'),ex(3,'A soft-stemmed herb grew back in the garden each spring.','一种茎柔软的草本植物每年春天都会在花园里重新生长。')],mistakes:[m('The cook added herbs to the soup, but no plants or seasonings were added.','The cook added salt to the soup, but no herbs or other seasonings were added.','added herbs 与没有加入任何植物或调味料矛盾；改用另一种调味料并对应否定。')],quiz:[q('herb',1,1,'A cook adds fresh herbs to soup mainly to?','add flavor','measure the soup’s height','make the bowl waterproof','香草常用于给食物调味。'),q('herb',2,2,'A medicinal herb is a plant used?','as a traditional remedy','to steer a boat','to build a fireplace','herb 可指药草或草药。'),q('herb',3,3,'A plant with a soft stem that dies back each year is botanically?','an herb','a metal hedge','a stone fruit','herb 也指茎柔软、每年枯萎的草本植物。'),q('herb',1,1,'Which phrase is natural in a recipe?','add mixed herbs','add a mixed herbingly','add herbs of mixedly','mixed herbs 是常见调味料搭配。')]});
D('herd',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'The hikers waited for the herd to cross the road before moving on.','徒步者们等一群牲畜过了路才继续前行。'),ex(3,'Ranchers herded the cattle into a fenced pasture at sunset.','日落时，牧场主把牛群赶进了围栏牧场。'),ex(4,'The fans herded toward the gate when the concert ended.','音乐会结束时，粉丝们成群地涌向大门。')],mistakes:[m('The shepherd herded the sheep away from the pen and left them inside it.','The shepherd herded the sheep into the pen and left them inside it.','away from 与 inside it 的方向矛盾；改为 into。')],quiz:[q('herd',1,1,'A herd of elephants is?','a large group of elephants','one elephant’s footprint','a flock of birds','herd 作名词可指一群同类动物。'),q('herd',2,2,'“He avoided the herd” may refer critically to?','a crowd of people who follow others','a single farm animal','a family’s inheritance','herd 可带贬义地指盲从的人群。'),q('herd',3,3,'Ranchers herd cattle into a pen by?','driving or guiding the animals together','planting vegetables around them','measuring each animal’s height','herd 作及物动词表示放牧、驱赶牲畜。'),q('herd',4,4,'After the concert, fans herded toward the exit. They?','moved together as a crowd','stayed alone in separate rooms','flew above the building','herd 也可表示人群聚集或成群移动。')]});
D('herder',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The herder led the goats to a shaded pasture for the afternoon.','牧民把山羊带到一处有树荫的牧场度过下午。')],mistakes:[m('The herder spent each day tending cattle but never looked after or guided them.','The herder spent each day tending cattle and guided them to pasture.','herder 指照料牲畜的人；若不放牧照管，则更适合称 visitor。')],quiz:[q('herder',1,1,'A herder’s work mainly involves?','tending farm animals','designing courtroom rules','repairing a helicopter rotor','herder 是放养牲畜的人。'),q('herder',1,1,'A herder may guide sheep toward?','pasture and water','a courtroom hearing','a city’s central office','牧民常把牲畜带到牧场和水源处。'),q('herder',1,1,'Which word is closest to herder?','shepherd','heir','herald','shepherd 是牧羊人，与 herder 意思接近。'),q('herder',1,1,'A group of herders is most likely working with?','livestock','office printers','ship steering wheels','herder 的工作对象是牲畜。')]});
D('here',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Leave your umbrella here beside the front desk.','把你的伞留在前台旁边这里。'),ex(2,'Bring the signed form here before the office closes.','办公室关门前把签好的表格拿到这里来。'),ex(3,'Here is the receipt you asked for.','这是你要的收据。'),ex(4,'Here the report turns from the causes to the proposed remedies.','报告在此处从原因转向提出的补救措施。')],mistakes:[m('Please put the box there beside me, where I am standing.','Please put the box here beside me, where I am standing.','说话人身边的位置是 here，不是 there；替换指示副词即可。')],quiz:[q('here',1,1,'“Put the keys here” tells someone to put them?','in this place','at a distant place','inside a different person','here 表示说话者所在的地方。'),q('here',2,2,'“Bring the documents here” asks someone to move them?','toward this place','away from this place','back to last year','here 可表示朝说话者所在处移动。'),q('here',3,3,'At a counter, “Here is your ticket” means?','this is the ticket being handed to you','the ticket is lost far away','the ticket belongs to the speaker’s sister','here is 可用于递交或指出某物。'),q('here',4,4,'In a presentation, “Here the argument changes” means?','at this point in the discussion','in a distant town','after the next century','here 也可指论述或时间进程中的这一点。')]});
D('hereafter',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Hereafter, all invoices should be sent to the new address.','今后，所有发票都应寄往新地址。')],mistakes:[m('Hereafter, the old procedure will remain in force only yesterday and not at all in the future.','Before today, the old procedure remained in force; hereafter, the new procedure will apply.','hereafter 指从现在起或以后，不能修饰仅发生在昨天的事；改写时间范围。')],quiz:[q('hereafter',1,1,'“Hereafter, keep the gate locked” means?','from now on, keep it locked','it was locked long ago','unlock it every morning','hereafter 可表示从今以后。'),q('hereafter',1,1,'A writer may use hereafter to mean?','in the life or period that follows','at a place nearby','in a group of animals','hereafter 也可指此后的时期或来世。'),q('hereafter',1,1,'Which phrase is close in meaning to hereafter?','from this point onward','the day before yesterday','at this exact location','from this point onward 表示此后。'),q('hereafter',1,1,'Which sentence uses hereafter correctly?','Hereafter, the company will publish its prices online.','Hereafter, the company published its prices last year only.','Hereafter, the company is located over there.','hereafter 表示从此以后，适用于未来持续的安排。')]});
D('hereby',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'I hereby authorize the clinic to release my test results to Dr. Chen.','本人特此授权诊所将检测结果交给陈医生。'),ex(2,'The parties hereby agree to revise the delivery schedule.','双方特此同意修改交付日程。')],mistakes:[m('I hereby deny the request, but this statement does not deny or decide anything.','I hereby deny the request, and this statement formally records that decision.','hereby 表示凭借本声明作出行为；说声明既否认又不作任何决定前后冲突。')],quiz:[q('hereby',1,1,'In a formal letter, “I hereby confirm” means?','I confirm by this statement','I confirmed it last year','I ask someone else to confirm','hereby 指凭借本声明或文件做出某事。'),q('hereby',2,2,'“The parties hereby agree” means the parties?','formally agree through this document','may agree sometime in the past','refuse to make any agreement','hereby 可表示借此正式约定。'),q('hereby',1,1,'Which document is most likely to use hereby?','a contract or official declaration','a casual greeting to a friend','a recipe for soup','hereby 属正式法律、公文语体。'),q('hereby',1,1,'Choose the natural collocation.','I hereby declare the meeting open.','I hereby at declare the meeting open.','I hereby declaredly the meeting open.','I hereby declare 是自然的正式表达。')]});
D('herewith',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Please find the signed consent form herewith.','随函附上已签署的同意书。')],mistakes:[m('I sent the receipt herewith, but it is being mailed separately next month.','I sent the receipt separately, and I will mail it next month.','herewith 表示随这封信一同寄出，与下月另寄相矛盾；换为 separately。')],quiz:[q('herewith',1,1,'A formal letter says “I enclose the report herewith.” The report is?','included with this letter','stored in a different office','scheduled to be written next year','herewith 表示随函附上。'),q('herewith',1,1,'Which phrase is closest to herewith?','along with this letter','from this point onward','for this reason','herewith 意为随同这封信一起。'),q('herewith',1,1,'Which context best fits herewith?','a formal message enclosing a signed form','a spoken greeting to a neighbor','a description of a herd crossing a field','herewith 多见于正式函件中的附件说明。'),q('herewith',1,1,'Choose the natural sentence.','I return the completed form herewith.','I return herewithly the completed form.','I herewith to return the completed form.','herewith 作副词，常置于正式句子中表示随函附上。')]});
D('heritage',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The festival celebrates the music and food that form the region’s heritage.','这个节日庆祝构成当地文化传承的音乐与饮食。'),ex(2,'The old harbor is a protected heritage site visited by school groups.','这座旧港口是受保护的遗产地，常有学生团体来访。')],mistakes:[m('The town’s heritage consists only of customs invented last week and has no link to the past.','The town’s heritage includes customs passed down from earlier generations.','heritage 指从过去传承下来的文化，不能只由上周才创造且与过去无关的习俗构成。')],quiz:[q('heritage',1,1,'A region’s cultural heritage includes?','traditions and culture passed down through generations','only the newest buildings in the region','a list of current weather reports','heritage 的常见义是代代相传的传统和文化。'),q('heritage',2,2,'A protected heritage site is usually?','a place valued for historical or cultural importance','a newly built parking space with no protection','a person legally inheriting property','heritage site 指受保护的文化或历史地点。'),q('heritage',1,1,'Which phrase is natural?','national heritage','heritageful nation','a heritage of the nationing','national heritage 是自然搭配。'),q('heritage',1,1,'How does heritage differ from inherited money?','It often refers to culture and traditions passed down.','It always means a bank account only.','It refers only to a future event.','heritage 多指文化传统，不等同于 inheritance 财产。')]});
D('hero',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The firefighters were hailed as heroes after rescuing the family.','消防员救出那家人后被誉为英雄。'),ex(2,'Her older sister was her hero and encouraged her to study science.','姐姐是她的偶像，鼓励她学习科学。'),ex(3,'The hero of the novel returns to his village at the end.','小说男主角在结尾时回到了自己的村庄。')],mistakes:[m('The hero risked his life to save the passengers, but everyone described him as a coward.','The hero risked his life to save the passengers, and everyone praised his courage.','英勇救人却被所有人称为懦夫不符合 hero 的赞誉义；改为赞扬勇气。')],quiz:[q('hero',1,1,'A person admired for a brave rescue may be called?','a hero','a heedless','a hectare','hero 可指因勇敢或高尚行为受敬佩的人。'),q('hero',2,2,'If a child says “My aunt is my hero,” the child means the aunt is?','someone greatly admired','the child’s legal heir','the main setting of a story','hero 也可指个人崇拜或钦佩的偶像。'),q('hero',3,3,'The hero of a novel is usually?','the main male character','the person who printed the book','the book’s final chapter','文学义 hero 可指作品中的男主角。'),q('hero',1,1,'Choose the correct plural of hero.','heroes','heros','heroies','hero 的复数通常拼作 heroes。')]});
D('heroic',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The neighbors made a heroic effort to pull the trapped dog from the floodwater.','邻居们奋力把困在洪水中的狗救了出来。')],mistakes:[m('The heroic firefighter ran away and refused to help anyone in danger.','The cowardly firefighter ran away and refused to help anyone in danger.','英勇救人的含义与逃避救援相反；改为 cowardly。')],quiz:[q('heroic',1,1,'A heroic rescue is?','very brave','carelessly planned','extremely expensive by definition','heroic 表示像英雄一样勇敢。'),q('heroic',1,1,'Which action is most likely heroic?','entering a burning room to rescue a child','leaving an injured person without help','hiding from a harmless noise','冒险救人体现英勇行为。'),q('heroic',1,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','a heroic effort','a heroical efforting','a heroically rescue','heroic 是可修饰 effort 的形容词。'),q('heroic',1,1,'Firefighters made heroic efforts. Their efforts were?','brave and admirable','slow because they lacked courage','unrelated to helping anyone','heroic 描写勇敢而值得敬佩的努力。')]});
D('heroin',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The public-health report describes the risks of heroin addiction.','这份公共卫生报告介绍了海洛因成瘾的风险。'),ex(2,'The clinic provides support for people recovering from heroin use.','这家诊所为正在戒除海洛因的人提供支持。')],mistakes:[m('The police report called the substance harmless because it was heroin, a highly addictive illegal drug.','The police report called the substance dangerous because it was heroin, a highly addictive illegal drug.','高成瘾性的非法毒品不能称为无害；把 harmless 改为 dangerous。')],quiz:[q('heroin',1,1,'Heroin is described in the entry as a drug made from?','morphine','sugar','salt water','词条将 heroin 说明为由吗啡制得的强效非法毒品。'),q('heroin',2,2,'In a public-health report, heroin use refers to?','using the illegal drug','using an ordinary cooking herb','wearing protective headgear','heroin use 指使用海洛因。'),q('heroin',1,1,'Heroin is highly?','addictive','nutritious','protective against falls','词条强调海洛因具有高度成瘾性。'),q('heroin',1,1,'Which word should not be confused with heroin?','heroine','hearth','hearing','heroine 是女英雄，拼写与 heroin 只差一个字母。')]});
D('hers',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The blue umbrella is hers, while the green one belongs to her brother.','蓝色雨伞是她的，绿色那把属于她哥哥。'),ex(2,'My notes are on the table, and hers are in the folder.','我的笔记在桌上，她的在文件夹里。')],mistakes:[m('This is hers coat, and the red coat belongs to her.','This is her coat, and the red coat is hers.','hers 是名词性物主代词，后面不直接接名词；应把 hers coat 改为 her coat。')],quiz:[q('hers',1,1,'“That seat is hers” means the seat belongs to?','her','the speaker','a group of children','hers 表示属于她的东西。'),q('hers',2,2,'“His bag is black; hers is brown” means hers replaces?','her bag','her brother','the brown color','hers 可代替前文提到的名词，如 her bag。'),q('hers',1,1,'Which sentence is correct?','The choice was hers.','The choice was hers one.','The choice her was.','名词性物主代词 hers 可以独立使用。'),q('hers',1,1,'Complete the contrast: My keys are here; ___ are upstairs.','hers','her','she','句中替代“她的钥匙”时要用 hers。')]});
D('herself',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Nora taught herself to repair the old radio.','诺拉自学修理那台旧收音机。'),ex(2,'The author herself introduced the final chapter at the event.','活动上由作者本人介绍了最后一章。'),ex(3,'After the fainting spell, she came to herself in the clinic.','昏厥后，她在诊所里苏醒过来。')],mistakes:[m('Nora blamed herself, although she was blaming her colleague instead.','Nora blamed her colleague, although she was blaming her colleague instead.','blame oneself 与责怪同事相矛盾；宾语应改为 her colleague。')],quiz:[q('herself',1,1,'“She cut herself” means?','she caused a cut to her own body','she cut another person','someone cut a piece from her dress','主语与宾语同为女性时用反身代词 herself。'),q('herself',2,2,'“The director herself answered the questions” emphasizes that?','the director personally answered','an assistant answered instead','the questions answered themselves','herself 可用于强调女性本人亲自做某事。'),q('herself',3,3,'After fainting, she came to herself means she?','regained consciousness','became a different person','left the room alone','come to herself 可表示苏醒、恢复知觉。'),q('herself',1,1,'Choose the correct phrase: She completed the task by ___.','herself','her','hers','by herself 可表示她独自完成。')]});
D('hesitant',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'He was hesitant about signing the contract before reading every clause.','读完每一条款之前，他对签合同仍有些犹豫。')],mistakes:[m('She felt hesitant about the choice and decided immediately without pausing or uncertainty.','She felt confident about the choice and decided immediately without pausing or uncertainty.','hesitant 表示犹豫，与毫不迟疑地立即决定相反；换成 confident。')],quiz:[q('hesitant',1,1,'A hesitant speaker may?','pause because she is unsure what to say','answer instantly with complete certainty','speak loudly to interrupt everyone','hesitant 指行动或说话前迟疑。'),q('hesitant',1,1,'If you are hesitant about accepting a job, you are?','uncertain whether to accept it','already working there for years','unable to hear the offer','hesitant about 表示对某事犹豫。'),q('hesitant',1,1,'Which word is closest to hesitant here?','uncertain','eager','decisive','hesitant 在此与 uncertain 意思接近。'),q('hesitant',1,1,'Choose the natural collocation.','hesitant about the plan','hesitant of the planly','hesitantly aboutness the plan','hesitant about 是自然搭配。')]});
D('hesitate',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'Please do not hesitate to contact the office if the parcel does not arrive.','如果包裹没有送到，请随时联系办公室。'),ex(3,'He hesitated over the unfamiliar name before reading it aloud.','读出这个陌生名字前，他支支吾吾地停顿了一下。')],mistakes:[m('She hesitated to answer because she was certain and had no doubts at all.','She hesitated to answer because she was uncertain and had doubts.','hesitate 表示因不确定而停顿，与毫无疑虑相反；改成 uncertain。')],quiz:[q('hesitate',1,1,'A person who hesitates before answering?','pauses because they are unsure','answers immediately with no pause','changes the subject without speaking','hesitate 可表示行动或说话前犹豫。'),q('hesitate',2,2,'“Don’t hesitate to ask” means?','feel free to ask','wait several years before asking','avoid asking under any circumstances','don’t hesitate to 是鼓励对方尽管做某事。'),q('hesitate',3,3,'If a speaker hesitates over a word, the speaker?','pauses and speaks uncertainly','writes the word in bold','already knows the word perfectly','hesitate over 可描述说话支吾、犹豫。'),q('hesitate',1,1,'Choose the correct past form.','hesitated','hesitatated','hesit','hesitate 的过去式为 hesitated。')]});
D('hey',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Hey, your notebook fell out of your bag.','嘿，你的笔记本从包里掉出来了。')],mistakes:[m('She shouted “Hey!” to greet her friend, but used it in a very formal legal contract.','She wrote “Dear Ms. Lee” to address her client in a formal legal letter.','hey 是口语化的呼喊或问候，不适合正式法律函件；换为正式称呼。')],quiz:[q('hey',1,1,'Someone calls “Hey, wait!” to?','get another person’s attention','announce an official law','describe a unit of land','hey 可用于喊人或引起注意。'),q('hey',1,1,'Which setting best fits “Hey, Sam!”?','a casual greeting','a formal court document','a scientific measurement','hey 是口语化招呼。'),q('hey',1,1,'Which interjection is closest in use to hey?','hi','henceforth','hearth','hi 可作为非正式问候，与 hey 用法接近。'),q('hey',1,1,'A friend says “Hey, how are you?” The word hey functions as?','a greeting','a noun meaning inheritance','an adjective meaning very ugly','hey 在这里是问候语。')]});
D('hi',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Hi, Ben! I have not seen you since the semester began.','嗨，本！这学期开学以来我还没见过你。'),ex(2,'Hi, over here! The taxi is waiting by the corner.','喂，我在这儿！出租车在街角等着。')],mistakes:[m('She wrote “Hi” to a close friend, using it as a formal legal closing after her signature.','She wrote “Hi” to a close friend as an informal greeting at the start of the message.','hi 是非正式问候，不能作正式信件的签名后落款；改为开头问候。')],quiz:[q('hi',1,1,'“Hi, nice to meet you” is?','an informal greeting','a formal court judgment','a unit for measuring area','hi 是非正式的见面问候。'),q('hi',2,2,'Someone calls “Hi, over here!” They are?','trying to attract attention','saying goodbye on the phone','describing a high building','hi 也可用于引起注意、喊人。'),q('hi',1,1,'Which is a casual way to greet a friend?','say hi to Kim','say hers to Kim','say hi-tech Kim','say hi to someone 是自然搭配。'),q('hi',1,1,'Compared with hello, hi is generally?','more informal','a legal term','a past tense verb','hi 比 hello 更随意。')]});
D('hi-tech',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The research team installed hi-tech sensors throughout the greenhouse.','研究团队在整座温室里安装了高科技传感器。')],mistakes:[m('The hi-tech lab used no modern machines, tools, or technology at all.','The traditional lab used no modern machines, tools, or technology at all.','hi-tech 表示使用新技术，与完全不用现代技术矛盾；改用 traditional。')],quiz:[q('hi-tech',1,1,'A hi-tech device uses?','new or advanced technology','only hand-carved wooden parts','no tools or machines','hi-tech 表示采用新技术或先进技术的。'),q('hi-tech',1,1,'A hi-tech laboratory is most likely equipped with?','modern instruments and machines','only stone tools','a herd of farm animals','高科技实验室使用现代设备。'),q('hi-tech',1,1,'Which spelling is also commonly used for hi-tech?','high-tech','highly-tech','hi-techly','high-tech 是 hi-tech 的常见另一种拼法。'),q('hi-tech',1,1,'Which phrase is natural?','hi-tech equipment','hi-techly equipment','equipment of hi-techs','hi-tech 可作形容词修饰 equipment。')]});
D('hibernate',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Some bats hibernate in caves where the winter temperature stays stable.','一些蝙蝠在冬季温度稳定的洞穴里冬眠。'),ex(2,'During the renovation, we hibernated at home and rarely went out.','装修期间，我们窝在家里，几乎不出门。')],mistakes:[m('The bear hibernated through winter while remaining fully active and searching for food every hour.','The bear stayed active through winter, searching for food every hour.','冬眠与整个冬天保持活跃、每小时觅食矛盾；改为 stay active。')],quiz:[q('hibernate',1,1,'When a bear hibernates, it?','spends the winter in a dormant state','migrates to a tropical beach every day','stays fully active all winter','hibernate 可指某些动物冬季休眠。'),q('hibernate',2,2,'A person who hibernates at home all winter?','stays indoors inactive for a long period','works outdoors every day','moves to another country each week','比喻义 hibernate 指长期待在室内、不活动。'),q('hibernate',1,1,'Which animal behavior is called hibernation?','winter dormancy in some animals','a bird building a nest in spring','a herd crossing a road','hibernation 是动物冬眠的状态。'),q('hibernate',1,1,'Choose the correct past tense: The bats ___ in the cave.','hibernated','hibernateded','hibernat','hibernate 的过去式为 hibernated。')]});
D('hidden',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The hikers discovered a hidden path behind the waterfall.','徒步者们在瀑布后面发现了一条隐蔽的小路。')],mistakes:[m('The hidden camera was placed in plain view on a bright red sign, where everyone could see it.','The visible camera was placed in plain view on a bright red sign, where everyone could see it.','hidden 表示不易被看见，放在人人都能看到的地方应称 visible。')],quiz:[q('hidden',1,1,'A hidden door is?','kept out of sight','painted a bright color for everyone to see','a door that cannot open','hidden 表示隐藏、不被看见。'),q('hidden',1,1,'Hidden costs are costs that?','are not obvious at first','are printed in large letters on the cover','have already been paid by everyone','hidden 可比喻不易察觉或未明说的费用。'),q('hidden',1,1,'The hidden camera recorded the room. The camera was?','kept out of view','placed on a public display','used to play music','hidden camera 指隐蔽摄像机。'),q('hidden',1,1,'Hidden is the past participle form of which verb?','hide','heed','heat','hidden 是 hide 的不规则过去分词。')]});
D('hide',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'The fox hid behind the rock until the hikers passed.','狐狸躲在岩石后面，直到徒步者经过。'),ex(3,'She tried to hide her disappointment when the results were announced.','结果公布时，她试图掩饰自己的失望。'),ex(4,'The tanner stretched the cow hide to dry in the sun.','制革工把牛皮展开，放在阳光下晾干。')],mistakes:[m('He hid the key on the table in full view, where nobody could see it.','He hid the key under the floorboard, where nobody could see it.','把钥匙放在显眼处不算藏起来；移到看不见的地方是最小修正。')],quiz:[q('hide',1,1,'To hide a key is to put it somewhere?','it cannot easily be seen','everyone must see it','it will turn into a different key','hide 的及物义是把某物藏到看不见处。'),q('hide',2,2,'The cat hid behind the sofa. The cat?','went somewhere it could not be seen','placed the sofa in a cupboard','showed itself to everyone','hide 可不及物表示躲藏。'),q('hide',3,3,'He could not hide his anger means he could not?','keep his feeling from being seen','cover his body with a blanket','put his anger in a box','hide 可指掩饰事实或情绪。'),q('hide',4,4,'A cow hide is?','the animal’s skin','a type of cooking herb','a ship’s steering wheel','hide 作名词可指兽皮或皮革。')]});
D('hideous',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The abandoned factory was a hideous sight against the otherwise beautiful hillside.','废弃工厂映衬在原本秀丽的山坡上，显得十分刺眼难看。')],mistakes:[m('The hideous mask was admired by everyone as beautifully elegant and pleasant to look at.','The elegant mask was admired by everyone as beautiful and pleasant to look at.','hideous 表示极丑或骇人，与美丽优雅相反；换成 elegant。')],quiz:[q('hideous',1,1,'A hideous mask is?','very ugly or shocking','perfectly ordinary and invisible','a highly advanced machine','hideous 表示非常丑陋或令人震惊。'),q('hideous',1,1,'Which might be called a hideous sight?','a ruined building covered in toxic waste','a clean garden in spring','a well-lit reading room','令人震惊难看的景象可称 hideous。'),q('hideous',1,1,'Choose a close synonym for hideous.','ugly','elegant','helpful','ugly 与 hideous 意思接近。'),q('hideous',1,1,'The adjective hideous can describe?','a shocking crime as well as an ugly object','only a person’s height','only a unit of land','hideous 可形容丑恶、骇人的事物或行为。')]});
D('hierarchy',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'The hospital hierarchy approved the new emergency procedure.','医院管理层批准了新的急救程序。'),ex(3,'The course explains the hierarchy of needs before discussing motivation.','课程先解释需求层次，再讨论动机。')],mistakes:[m('The company has no hierarchy, so every employee is ranked above the chief executive.','The company has a hierarchy, so some roles rank above others.','hierarchy 指存在层级排序；所有人都高于首席执行官与之不符。')],quiz:[q('hierarchy',1,1,'A workplace hierarchy organizes people by?','status or authority','shoe size','the order of their birthdays only','hierarchy 可指按地位或权力划分的等级体系。'),q('hierarchy',2,2,'The party hierarchy refers to?','the senior leaders of the party','all the voters in the country','the party’s printed logo','hierarchy 也可指组织的领导层。'),q('hierarchy',3,3,'A hierarchy of needs arranges needs?','in levels or ranks','in alphabetical order only','by the colors of a chart','hierarchy 可指按层次排列的结构。'),q('hierarchy',1,1,'Choose the correct plural.','hierarchies','hierarchys','hierarchyes','以辅音字母加 y 结尾的 hierarchy 复数为 hierarchies。')]});
D('high',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'The mountain pass remained closed because of high winds.','山口因大风而持续关闭。'),ex(4,'The singer reached a high note without strain.','歌手毫不费力地唱到了一个高音。'),ex(5,'The company’s sales hit a new high in June.','公司销售额在六月创下新高。')],mistakes:[m('The high wall measured only ten centimetres from the ground to the top.','The low wall measured only ten centimetres from the ground to the top.','只有十厘米高的墙不能称作 high wall；换成 low。')],quiz:[q('high',1,1,'A wall that is two metres high has?','a large bottom-to-top measurement','a large amount of money','a sound near the top of a musical range','high 可描述物体的垂直高度。'),q('high',2,2,'A high price means the price is?','large or expensive','below the ground','a musical sound','high 可表示数量或程度大。'),q('high',3,3,'A high-ranking official has?','a senior position','a very tall hat only','a quiet voice','high 可描述地位或等级较高。'),q('high',4,4,'A high note is near the top of the range of?','sounds','land area','shoe sizes','音乐中的 high note 指音高较高的音。')]});
