D('high-rise',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The new high-rise has thirty floors and a shared rooftop garden.','这栋新建的高层建筑有三十层，并设有共享屋顶花园。')],mistakes:[m('They moved into a high-rise, a one-storey cottage with a low roof.','They moved into a cottage, a one-storey home with a low roof.','high-rise 指很高的建筑，与一层低矮小屋矛盾；换成 cottage。')],quiz:[q('high-rise',1,1,'A high-rise is?','a very tall building','a one-storey shed','a low stone wall','high-rise 可作名词指高层建筑。'),q('high-rise',1,1,'People living in a high-rise usually live?','in a building with many floors','inside a small tent','under a bridge only','高层建筑通常有许多楼层。'),q('high-rise',1,1,'Which word is close in meaning to high-rise?','skyscraper','hearth','hedge','skyscraper 也指高楼或摩天大楼。'),q('high-rise',1,1,'Which phrase uses high-rise as an adjective?','a high-rise apartment building','an apartment high-risingly','a high-rises apartment building','high-rise 可作定语修饰 apartment building。')]});
